{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1370100-asking-for-help-with-understanding-a-couple-of-rules","id":1370100,"title":"Asking for help with understanding a couple of rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-24T11:04:29-08:00","id":1370100,"title":"Asking for help with understanding a couple of rules","content":"I posted this on the Onyx Path Reddit and haven't gotten any answers in a few days so I thought I would try here.<ul><li>Do characters with stamina 3 + get extra bruised beyond what is on the character sheet or do characters only start with a certain amount of each (I can't find the exact starting amounts, just the general statement on page 98 under the Health Section).</li> <li>How do contacts get created? Do you choose contacts based on your Paths and then you can use those when you invoke your path or do you create the contacts on the fly? If created during the session does the contact get created at 2 dots to use, then that contact keeps those dots until end of session, then if that path is invoked again you can get another 2 dots to spend on that contact or another contact under that path? I am just not quite sure how this is supposed to work in practice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10979-phorden","name":"phorden","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T11:13:19-08:00","id":1370102,"title":"","content":"Health: You have one Bruised, one Injured, one Maimed, and one Taken Out injury condition level to start with. Higher Stamina adds to those.<br /> <br /> I'm not as familiar with Paths in Scion. So I won't 